            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "RbyqI",
              "name": "Spacer",
              "width": 10,
              "height": 56
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "sMk0i",
              "name": "Field",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "GYSEC",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "WE ARE ALL FUCKED: AN ANDROID DEVELO",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "HUMANS"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "WE ARE ALL FUCKED: AN ANDROID DEVELOPER’S GUIDE TO THE POST-AI APOCALYPSE"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "AI is dominating Android development, driven by hype over reality. As organizations rush chatbot syntax into production, we are left cleaning up a dumpster fire of unscalable slop. It is time to look past the echo chamber and address our real challenge: protecting codebases from automated pollution. True engineering relies on architectural rigor and knowing what not to buil…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Ashley Davies"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "ddwO8",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "GENUI IN PRODUCTION: HOW GENUI AND A",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "GENUI IN PRODUCTION: HOW GENUI AND A2UI CHANGE MOBILE APPS"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "AI has made it easier to ship apps but not easier to make apps people keep using. The apps that matter will be the ones that fit the person opening them. GenUI is a key enabler in this direction: the design system stays stable while the UI adapts to the user. We will go from idea to architecture: what GenUI actually is (and is not), how the A2UI protocol makes it backend provid…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Cagatay Ulusoy"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "H1xV7",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "GENUI, LLMS DRIVING THE USER EXPERIE",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "GENUI, LLMS DRIVING THE USER EXPERIENCE, WHAT COULD GO WRONG"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Current LLMs and models are powerful enough to generate real-time, context-based interfaces for each user. This talk will explore the benefits of providing each user with a personalized interface far beyond what has been possible until now. It will also address the challenges this entails, not only in terms of technology, but also…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Juan Delgado, Brian Egan"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "nwi6e",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "YOUR APP, THEIR DATA: LOCAL-FIRST WI",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "OPEN SOURCE"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "YOUR APP, THEIR DATA: LOCAL-FIRST WITH EVOLU"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Most apps store users’ data on a server and lend it back through an API. Local-first reverses that model: data lives on the user’s device first and remains under their control. The app works without a connection—and can outlive both its servers and the company behind it. To bring this approach to Trezor Suite across web, desktop, and mobile, we used Evolu: local SQLite, CRDTs, an…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Matěj Kříž"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "ulExW",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "GEMINI ENTERPRISE IN PRACTICE: FROM ",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "GEMINI ENTERPRISE IN PRACTICE: FROM SECURE ACCESS TO REAL BUSINESS IMPACT"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Gemini Enterprise brings generative AI into the workplace—but adopting it successfully requires more than just enabling a tool. In this talk, we explore how Gemini Enterprise fits into real organisational environments, focusing on secure access, identity integration, data boundaries, and practical usage patterns. Rather than product demos, we’ll loo…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Dr Roushanak Rahmat"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "qHaZb",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "IS YOUR REPO AGENT-READY? BUILDING A",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "IS YOUR REPO AGENT-READY? BUILDING A CHECKLIST FOR THE AI REVOLUTION"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Have you heard of AI? Of course you have – it’s likely writing code alongside you every day. But as we move from basic autocompletion to autonomous AI agents, a critical question arises: is your codebase actually built to collaborate with them? In this talk, I will share my journey of trying to build the ultimate, universal checklist for optimizing repositories for AI…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Dominika Zając"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "pkgzd",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "BRIGHT FUTURE FOR SOFTWARE DEVELOPME",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "HUMANS"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "BRIGHT FUTURE FOR SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT (AND WHY MY DEVELOPERS DISAGREE)"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "This is not a talk about AI. It is a talk about the people who have to live with it, and about what the new way of work actually costs them. I spend my days designing future – a system where AI agents write most of our software. This is a fundamental change to digital product building and many people are afraid of what’s next. I will show you what impacts my (and probably…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Filip Kirschner"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "xdFfW",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "INTERACTIONS THAT WORK FOR ALL USERS",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "OPEN SOURCE"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "INTERACTIONS THAT WORK FOR ALL USERS"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "This talk explores how users interact with websites and how developers can make those interactions accessible to everyone. Using practical examples, such as converting an inaccessible navigation widget or carousel into accessible versions, we’ll explore common accessibility issues and their solutions. The session will include multiple coding demonstrations to…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Anuradha Kumari"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "zfpZM",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "BUILDING A REAL-TIME COLLABORATIVE E",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "OPEN SOURCE"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "BUILDING A REAL-TIME COLLABORATIVE EDITOR"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Have you ever wondered what it takes to develop a solution similar to Google Docs and then build on top of it with extra layers of security and functionality? During the planning phase of a military operation, there are multiple text documents that need to be updated simultaneously by multiple users. At the same time, there is a requirement to provi…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Mihaela Gheorghe-Roman"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "qDjPd",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "THE DAY I LEFT MY LINUX MACHINE RUNN",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "THE DAY I LEFT MY LINUX MACHINE RUNNING: A LOVE STORY WITH OPENCLAW & HERMES"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "One evening I left an agent running on my Linux box with a vague task and went to sleep. What happened next is a story about agents that ship, agents that break things, and what it takes to trust a machine with your shell. Practical, opinionated, and full of scars…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Riccardo Carlesso"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "Od8br",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "NOT ALL APIS ARE CREATED EQUAL: THE ",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "HUMANS"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "NOT ALL APIS ARE CREATED EQUAL: THE MOST USEFUL SKILL FOR 2026"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "The most valuable interface you will work with this year is not an SDK. It is a person. A talk about the skills that make engineers effective in rooms where the other side does not speak code, and why that matters more as the code itself gets cheaper…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Zuzana Pešková, Filip Goszler"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "PmqJE",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "CAN AN LLM UNDERSTAND YOUR CAR? REAL",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "CAN AN LLM UNDERSTAND YOUR CAR? REAL TELEMETRY AND PREDICTIVE INSIGHTS"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Cars produce a firehose of telemetry. What happens when you point a language model at it? This talk walks through a real pipeline from CAN bus to LLM: what the model gets right, where it hallucinates, and how to build predictive insights that a driver can actually trust…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Soumaya Erradi"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "y5Yjw",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "HARDWARE IS HARD, BUT AI IS SMARTER:",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "HUMANS"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "HARDWARE IS HARD, BUT AI IS SMARTER: THE ROBOTICS \"IPHONE MOMENT\" IS HERE"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Robotics has been ten years away for thirty years. That is changing. A product-and-design look at why foundation models are the missing piece, what the first mass-market robots will feel like, and what it means for the people who design and build them…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Adi Mazor Kario"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "DzFdR",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "OPEN SESAME TO THE MONOLITH: RAIDING",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "OPEN SESAME TO THE MONOLITH: RAIDING THE LEGACY CAVE WITH AI AGENTS"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Every enterprise sits on a 'Cave of Wonders'. A massive codebase packed with decades of invaluable business logic, hardened edge cases, and customer data. But it is usually locked behind outdated languages, undocumented dependencies, and crushing technical debt. For years, engineers have been forced to act as poor woodcutters, endlessly chopping away at Jira tickets jus…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Abdel Sghiouar"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "T8X6Ki",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "AI PRINTER GO BRRR",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "AI PRINTER GO BRRR"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Every AI demo works fine until it has to touch something real. The model responds, the screenshot looks great, and then you try to wire it up to an actual device and find out how much the screen was covering for you. So we figured we'd close that gap in front of an audience instead of quietly at home. One prompt, one Genkit flow running on…"
                    },
                    "X6C58": {
                      "fill": "$panel-lit"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Dominik Šimoník, Denis Valášek"
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "HhAuK",
          "type": "ref",
          "ref": "NdYne",
          "name": "Closer",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "descendants": {
